{%- liquid
  assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign on_sale = false
  if v.compare_at_price > v.price
    assign on_sale = true
    comment
      floor, not round. 49.99 against 79.99 is 37.5% off, and round turns that
      into "38% off" - a discount claim slightly larger than the real one, on
      a page built for paid ads. Rounding a saving DOWN is always safe.
    endcomment
    assign save_pct = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: v.compare_at_price | floor
    assign save_amt = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price
  endif

  comment
    No fallback rating here either - see the note in snippets/product-card.
    The JSON-LD block at the bottom of this file only emits aggregateRating
    when rating_count is real, and feeding Google a made-up 4.8 is how a
    domain loses its rich results, so the two must not disagree.
  endcomment
  assign rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating
  if rating == blank and settings.card_use_fallback_rating
    assign rating = settings.card_fallback_rating
  endif
  assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | default: 0
  assign sold = product.metafields.custom.sold_count.value

  assign hook = product.metafields.custom.hook.value | default: product.metafields.custom.short_description.value

  comment
    Bullets are optional. With no metafield we take the first sentences of the
    description, so a product imported with nothing but a title, a price, a
    photo and a paragraph still produces a finished page. Written detail is an
    upgrade, never a prerequisite for shipping.
  endcomment
  assign bullets = product.metafields.custom.bullets.value
  assign li_source = ''
  if bullets == blank and product.description != blank
    if product.description contains '<li>'
      assign li_source = product.description
    else
      assign plain = product.description | strip_html | strip
      assign bullets = plain | split: '. '
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  If the description already HAS a list, use its items. Sentence-splitting a
  description that ends in a <ul> does not work: strip_html joins the list
  items with nothing at all between them, and list items do not end in a full
  stop, so `split: '. '` cannot see the joins. Every product page on the store
  was rendering its last bullet as all three run together -

    "Long line, drop shoulder, worn open. The same ribcage knit in green,
     pink, cream and black Long line, drop shoulder, made to be worn open
     Unisex sizing"

  - which looked like bad copy rather than a template bug, so it survived a
  whole round of review on a live storefront.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if li_source != '' -%}
  {%- capture bullet_list -%}
    {%- assign chunks = li_source | split: '<li>' -%}
    {%- for chunk in chunks offset: 1 -%}
      {%- assign one = chunk | split: '</li>' | first | strip_html | strip -%}
      {%- if one != blank -%}{{ one }}~|~{%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    remove_last first. Every item is written with a trailing separator, so the
    captured string ends in one, and `split` keeps the empty piece after it -
    which renders as a blank bullet with a tick beside it at the bottom of
    every product page.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign bullets = bullet_list | strip | remove_last: '~|~' | split: '~|~' -%}
{%- endif -%}

<section class="pdp">
  <div class="wrap pdp__in">

    {%- comment -%} ---------------- gallery ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="pdp__gal">
      <div class="pdp__stage" id="stage">
        {%- if on_sale and section.settings.show_save -%}
          <span class="pdp__off">Save {{ save_pct }}%</span>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if product.featured_media -%}
          <img id="stageimg"
               src="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 900 }}"
               alt="{{ product.featured_media.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
               width="900" height="900" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
        {%- else -%}
          {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'pdp__ph' }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
        <div class="pdp__thumbs" id="thumbs">
          {%- for media in product.media limit: 8 -%}
            <button class="pdp__thumb{% if forloop.first %} on{% endif %}" type="button"
                    data-full="{{ media | image_url: width: 900 }}"
                    aria-label="View image {{ forloop.index }}">
              <img src="{{ media | image_url: width: 220 }}"
                   alt="{{ media.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
                   width="220" height="220" loading="lazy">
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------------- buy box ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="pdp__buy">
      <nav class="pdp__crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span>/</span>
        {%- if collection -%}
          <a href="{{ collection.url }}">{{ collection.title }}</a><span>/</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {{ product.title }}
      </nav>

      <h1 class="pdp__h">{{ product.title }}</h1>

      {%- if section.settings.show_rating and rating != blank -%}
        <div class="pdp__rate">
          {%- if rating_count > 0 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The count is a LINK to the reviews further down the page. It is
              the one piece of proof on this screen a sceptical shopper will
              want to check, so checking it should be one tap.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- capture rc -%}
              {{ rating | round: 1 }} &middot; <a href="#reviews">{% render 'thousands', n: rating_count %} review{% unless rating_count == 1 %}s{% endunless %}</a>
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {% render 'stars', rating: rating, count: rc, cls: 'pdp__rc' %}
          {%- else -%}
            {% render 'stars', rating: rating %}
            <span class="pdp__rc">{{ rating | round: 1 }} out of 5</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if sold != blank and sold > 0 -%}
            <span class="pdp__sold">{% render 'thousands', n: sold %}+ sold</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if hook != blank -%}
        <p class="pdp__hook">{{ hook }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="pdp__price">
        <span class="price" id="pprice">{{ v.price | money }}</span>
        {%- if on_sale -%}
          <span class="was" id="pwas">{{ v.compare_at_price | money }}</span>
          <span class="pdp__save">You save {{ save_amt | money }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if bullets != blank -%}
        <ul class="pdp__bul">
          {%- for b in bullets limit: 5 -%}
            {%- assign line = b | strip | strip_html -%}
            {%- if line != blank -%}
              <li>{{ line }}</li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_stock and v.inventory_management != blank and v.inventory_quantity > 0 and v.inventory_quantity <= section.settings.low_stock -%}
        {%- assign pct = v.inventory_quantity | times: 100 | divided_by: section.settings.low_stock -%}
        <div class="pdp__stock">
          <div class="pdp__bar"><i style="width:{{ pct }}%"></i></div>
          {%- comment -%}
            The real number when Shopify is tracking it, otherwise the wording
            from Theme settings. Empty that setting and the line disappears
            from all 52 pages at once.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p>Only {{ v.inventory_quantity }} left in stock</p>
        </div>
      {%- elsif section.settings.show_stock and settings.urgency_text != blank -%}
        <div class="pdp__stock">
          <div class="pdp__bar"><i style="width:22%"></i></div>
          <p>{{ settings.urgency_text | escape }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- form 'product', product, id: 'buyform', class: 'pdp__form' -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="id" id="vid" value="{{ v.id }}">

        {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
          <div class="pdp__opts" id="opts">
            {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
              <div class="opt" data-idx="{{ forloop.index0 }}">
                <span class="opt__label">{{ option.name }}: <b data-sel>{{ option.selected_value }}</b></span>
                <div class="opt__vals">
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    <label class="pill{% if value == option.selected_value %} on{% endif %}">
                      <input type="radio"
                             name="opt-{{ forloop.parentloop.index0 }}"
                             value="{{ value | escape }}"
                             {% if value == option.selected_value %}checked{% endif %}>
                      <span>{{ value }}</span>
                    </label>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endunless -%}

        <div class="pdp__act">
          <div class="qty" id="qty">
            <button type="button" data-q="-1" aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
            <b id="qtyn">1</b>
            <button type="button" data-q="1" aria-label="Increase quantity">&plus;</button>
          </div>
          <input type="hidden" name="quantity" id="qtyi" value="1">

          {%- comment -%}
            Add to cart is the OUTLINE button here and Buy It Now below is the
            gold one - deliberately the reverse of the single-button layout
            this replaced. A product page taking cold ad traffic is trying to
            close one sale, not build a basket.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            data-add carries the wording, because the button's own text is not
            a safe place to read it back from: on a variant that is sold out
            the button starts life saying "Sold out". Without this the first
            time a shopper switched variant the label reverted to a hardcoded
            "Add to cart" and the setting above was silently discarded.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button class="btn btn--add btn--out" type="submit" id="buybtn"
                  data-add="{{ settings.add_to_cart_text | default: 'Add to Cart' | escape }}"
                  {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
            {%- if v.available -%}{{ settings.add_to_cart_text | default: 'Add to Cart' }}{%- else -%}Sold out{%- endif -%}
          </button>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Buy It Now: adds this one item and goes straight to checkout, skipping
          the cart. It is a plain button rather than Shopify's dynamic checkout
          button on purpose - the dynamic one only renders when accelerated
          checkout is switched on for the store AND the customer's browser
          offers a wallet, so on a brand new store it is frequently just absent.
          This one is always there. Turn on the dynamic buttons as well below if
          you want Shop Pay and PayPal underneath it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.show_buy_now and v.available -%}
          <button class="btn btn--gold btn--wide btn--buynow js-buynow" type="button"
                  data-vid="{{ v.id }}">
            {{ section.settings.buy_now_text | default: 'Buy It Now' }}
          </button>
          {%- if section.settings.buy_now_note != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp__bnote">{{ section.settings.buy_now_note | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The express wallet button. This renders ONE wallet, and the theme
          does not get to say which: Shopify sends the choice down in the
          <shopify-accelerated-checkout> element as `recommended`, picked from
          Settings > Payments > Shopify Payments > Manage > Wallets and then
          filtered by what the shopper's own device supports.

          So "replace Shop Pay with Apple Pay and Google Pay" is a Settings
          change, not a code change. Hiding <shop-pay-wallet-button> with CSS
          from here does NOT promote the next wallet - Shopify has already
          decided, and the slot would simply render empty.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.show_dynamic_checkout -%}
          {{ form | payment_button }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endform -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The four delivery promises come from Theme settings > Shipping &
        guarantees, so they are written once and repeated on all 52 product
        pages from there. Adding "Assurance" blocks to this section replaces
        them, for the case where one product genuinely ships differently.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture assurances -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'assurance' and block.settings.text != blank -%}
            <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ block.settings.text | escape }}</li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if assurances contains '<li' -%}
        <ul class="pdp__trust">{{ assurances }}</ul>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- capture globals -%}
          {%- if settings.ship_free != blank -%}<li>{{ settings.ship_free | escape }}</li>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if settings.ship_guarantee != blank -%}<li>{{ settings.ship_guarantee | escape }}</li>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if settings.ship_dispatch != blank -%}<li>{{ settings.ship_dispatch | escape }}</li>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if settings.ship_returns != blank -%}<li>{{ settings.ship_returns | escape }}</li>{%- endif -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if globals contains '<li' -%}
          <ul class="pdp__trust">{{ globals }}</ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/json" id="variant-data">
    {{ product.variants | json }}
  </script>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------------- features ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign features = product.metafields.custom.features.value -%}
{%- if features != blank -%}
  <section class="sec sec--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="sec__k">Why it works</p>
      <h2 class="sec__h">{{ section.settings.features_heading | escape }}</h2>
      <div class="feats">
        {%- for f in features limit: 6 -%}
          {%- assign parts = f | split: '|' -%}
          <div class="feat rv">
            <h3>{{ parts[0] | strip }}</h3>
            {%- if parts[1] -%}<p>{{ parts[1] | strip }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------------- description, specs, in the box ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign specs = product.metafields.custom.specs.value -%}
{%- assign in_box = product.metafields.custom.in_the_box.value -%}

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap spec">
    <div class="spec__tbl">
      <h2 class="sec__h">{{ section.settings.details_heading | escape }}</h2>

      {%- if product.description != blank -%}
        <div class="rte">{{ product.description }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <table>
        <tbody>
          {%- if specs != blank -%}
            {%- for s in specs -%}
              {%- assign parts = s | split: '|' -%}
              <tr><th>{{ parts[0] | strip }}</th><td>{{ parts[1] | strip }}</td></tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Rows Shopify already knows. They fill the table for a product whose
            spec metafield was never written.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if product.type != blank -%}
            <tr><th>Category</th><td>{{ product.type }}</td></tr>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if product.vendor != blank -%}
            <tr><th>Brand</th><td>{{ product.vendor }}</td></tr>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if v.sku != blank -%}
            <tr><th>Item code</th><td>{{ v.sku }}</td></tr>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if v.weight > 0 -%}
            <tr><th>Weight</th><td>{{ v.weight | weight_with_unit: v.weight_unit }}</td></tr>
          {%- endif -%}
          <tr><th>Shipping</th><td>{{ section.settings.shipping_line | escape }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Returns</th><td>{{ section.settings.returns_line | escape }}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="spec__box">
      {%- if in_box != blank -%}
        <h2 class="sec__h">In the box</h2>
        <ul class="ticks">
          {%- for i in in_box -%}
            <li>{{ i }}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if product.featured_media -%}
        <img class="spec__art"
             src="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 500 }}"
             alt="{{ product.title | escape }}"
             width="500" height="500" loading="lazy">
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------------- sticky mobile buy bar ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="stick" id="stick" aria-hidden="true">
  {%- if product.featured_media -%}
    <img src="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 120 }}" alt="" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy">
  {%- endif -%}
  <div class="stick__m">
    <p>{{ product.title }}</p>
    <span>
      <b id="stickprice">{{ v.price | money }}</b>
      {%- if on_sale -%}<s>{{ v.compare_at_price | money }}</s>{%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>
  <button class="btn btn--add" type="button" id="stickadd" data-add="Add"
          {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
    {%- if v.available -%}Add{%- else -%}Sold out{%- endif -%}
  </button>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Product structured data, written out rather than left to a filter, so the
  fields are ours to control.

  aggregateRating is emitted ONLY when a reviews app has supplied a real count.
  The star rating on the page falls back to a default for products with no
  reviews yet, and putting that fallback into structured data would be telling
  Google about ratings that do not exist - which is exactly what gets rich
  results revoked for a whole domain.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org/",
  "@type": "Product",
  "name": {{ product.title | json }},
  "url": {{ request.origin | append: product.url | json }},
  {%- comment -%}
    Every photo, not just the featured one. Google's product rich result takes
    an array and shows more of it than one image; the products now arrive with
    five to eight photos each from the supplier gallery, so listing one was
    throwing away the other seven for free.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.images.size > 0 -%}
  "image": [
    {%- for img in product.images limit: 8 -%}
      {{ img | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: "https:" | json }}
      {%- unless forloop.last %},{% endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ],
  {%- endif -%}
  "description": {{ product.description | strip_html | truncate: 500 | json }},
  {%- if product.vendor != blank -%}
  "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ product.vendor | json }} },
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if v.sku != blank -%}
  "sku": {{ v.sku | json }},
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if rating_count > 0 -%}
  "aggregateRating": {
    "@type": "AggregateRating",
    "ratingValue": {{ rating | json }},
    "reviewCount": {{ rating_count | json }}
  },
  {%- endif -%}
  "offers": [
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
    {
      "@type": "Offer",
      {%- if variant.sku != blank -%}
      "sku": {{ variant.sku | json }},
      {%- endif -%}
      "availability": "https://schema.org/{% if variant.available %}InStock{% else %}OutOfStock{% endif %}",
      "price": {{ variant.price | divided_by: 100.0 | json }},
      "priceCurrency": {{ cart.currency.iso_code | json }},
      "url": {{ request.origin | append: variant.url | json }}
    }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product page",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_rating",
      "label": "Show star rating",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_save",
      "label": "Show the savings badge on the image",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Buy buttons"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_buy_now",
      "label": "Show a Buy It Now button",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Adds the item and goes straight to checkout, skipping the cart."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "buy_now_text",
      "label": "Buy It Now text",
      "default": "Buy It Now"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "buy_now_note",
      "label": "Small line under it",
      "default": "Straight to checkout - skips the cart"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_dynamic_checkout",
      "label": "Also show the express wallet button",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Shopify's own express button - Shop Pay, Apple Pay or Google Pay. WHICH one appears is not a theme setting: Shopify picks it in Settings > Payments > Shopify Payments > Manage > Wallets, and then only shows the one the shopper's device supports. Apple Pay renders in Safari on Apple hardware only, so it will never appear on a Windows PC no matter what is ticked here. Untick this to hide the row entirely; Buy It Now above always works."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Stock urgency"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_stock",
      "label": "Show a low-stock bar",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Only appears when Shopify is actually tracking inventory for the variant, so it can never show a number you cannot back up."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "low_stock",
      "label": "Show the bar under this many units",
      "min": 5,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "default": 25
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Headings"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "features_heading",
      "label": "Features heading",
      "default": "Built for the night"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "details_heading",
      "label": "Details heading",
      "default": "The details"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "shipping_line",
      "label": "Shipping row",
      "default": "Free US shipping, ships within 24 hours"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "returns_line",
      "label": "Returns row",
      "default": "30 days, no questions"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "assurance",
      "name": "Assurance line",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "Free US shipping on every order"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
